<title>INDIA: POLL-India SAIL 6-mth net seen sliding.</title>
<headline>POLL-India SAIL 6-mth net seen sliding.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net profit of state-run Steel Authority of India Ltd (SAIL) is projected to slide 69.8 percent to 1.1 billion rupees in the six months to September 30, 1997, a Reuter poll consensus showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The 18 top brokerages forecast sales to rise by an average 5.6 percent to 63.6 billion rupees.</p>
<p>Following are the details of the poll compared with actuals for the first half of 1996/97.</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>				NET PROFIT		   SALES</p>
<p>				   (first half to September 30)</p>
<p>			    97/98     96/97	97/98	96/97</p>
<p>					 (in millions of rupees)</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>SAIL   ----PAT seen down 69.8%, sales 5.6%</p>
<p>Average		1,091.46  3,614.50    63,637.05  67,441.30</p>
<p>High		   3,680.00		  84.768.00</p>
<p>Low		     -900.00		  52,965.00</p>
<p>--Bombay equities desk 91-22-265-9000</p>
